<PageTitle>Tree grid — FlexCore Showcase</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Tree grid" Category="Data Grid" CategoryHref="demo/grid" ControlName="TreeGridControl"
                   Tagline="A flat list with Id and ParentId columns, shown as a collapsible hierarchy."
                   SourcePath="Grid/TreeGridControl.razor;Grid/TreeGridControl.razor.cs;Grid/TreeGridControl.Checking.cs;Grid/TreeGridControl.Editing.cs;Grid/TreeGridControl.Frozen.cs;Grid/TreeGridControl.Loading.cs;Grid/TreeGridControl.Moving.cs;Grid/TreeGridControl.Query.cs;Grid/TreeGridColumn.cs;Grid/TreeGridMutationModels.cs;Grid/TreeGridQuery.cs;Grid/GridModels.cs;Grid/GridToolbarModels.cs;Grid/GridEnums.cs">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>TreeGridControl</code> builds the hierarchy from two property names on a flat list: <code>IdMapping</code> names the key and
            <code>ParentIdMapping</code> the parent key, null or empty for a root. <code>TreatAsParent</code> marks rows as expandable even
            before their children are in the list, <code>TreeColumnIndex</code> picks the column that carries the indentation and icons, <code>NodeExpandIconStyle</code> is
            <code>PlusMinus</code> or <code>Triangle</code>, <code>EnableCollapseAll</code> starts with every node collapsed unless an
            <code>InitialExpansionPredicate</code> says otherwise, and <code>ToggleOnRowClick="false"</code> limits mouse toggling to the icon; the keyboard still toggles. <code>Expanded</code> and <code>Collapsed</code> report the node
            and its level; <code>ExpandAllAsync</code> and <code>CollapseAllAsync</code> change the state from code without raising those events.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="airports" Title="4,009 airports, loaded as you open them" RazorCode="@Code.Airports" CSharpCode="@Code.AirportsCs">
            <Description><p>The airports from the <a href="demo/grid#airports">Data Grid</a> page as continent, country, airport and runway. Only the six continents are in <code>DataSource</code>; <code>TreatAsParent</code> marks the continents, countries and airports with runways as expandable, and <code>LoadChildren</code> returns a row's children the first time it opens, so a visitor who opens Portugal loads Portugal's nineteen airports and nothing else. Europe opens on load through <code>InitialExpansionPredicate</code>. Group rows count their airports and open runways and give the longest; a runway row gives its own length, surface and whether it is lighted. Click a header to sort; each level sorts within its parent. The line under the grid counts the rows loaded so far.</p></Description>
            <Controls>
                <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="@(() => _places?.CollapseAllAsync() ?? Task.CompletedTask)">Collapse all</ButtonControl>
            </Controls>
            <Demo>
                <TreeGridControl @ref="_places"
                                 TValue="Place"
                                 DataSource="@_continents"
                                 IdMapping="Id"
                                 ParentIdMapping="ParentId"
                                 TreeColumnIndex="0"
                                 TreatAsParent="@(p => p.Level < 2 || (p.Level == 2 && p.Runways > 0))"
                                 LoadChildren="LoadPlacesAsync"
                                 EnableCollapseAll="true"
                                 InitialExpansionPredicate="@(p => p.Name == "Europe")"
                                 AllowSorting="true"
                                 AllowSelection="true"
                                 Height="440px"
                                 Expanded="@(a => _last = $"opened {a.Data?.Name}")"
                                 Collapsed="@(a => _last = $"closed {a.Data?.Name}")">
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="@nameof(Place.Name)" HeaderText="Place" Width="340px" />
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="@nameof(Place.Detail)" HeaderText="Type or surface" Width="150px" />
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="@nameof(Place.Airports)" HeaderText="Airports" Width="80px" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Format="N0" />
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="@nameof(Place.Runways)" HeaderText="Runways" Width="80px" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Format="N0" />
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="@nameof(Place.LongestRunwayFt)" HeaderText="Longest runway (ft)" Width="140px" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Format="N0" />
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="@nameof(Place.ElevationFt)" HeaderText="Elevation (ft)" Width="110px" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Format="N0" />
                </TreeGridControl>
                <p class="result">@_loaded.ToString("N0") of @_total.ToString("N0") rows loaded@(_last is null ? "" : $" · last {_last}")</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
        <DemoExample Id="org" Title="Org chart: who reports to whom" RazorCode="@Code.Org" CSharpCode="@Code.OrgCs">
            <Description><p>Razor Sharp Getaways, an imagined tour operator: @_staff.Count(p => !p.Vacant).ToString("N0") people in @_staff.Count.ToString("N0") posts, from the chief executive to seasonal guides in twelve destinations and three contact centres. The staff come from a generator with a fixed seed, so everyone sees the same people, and every name is made up. Search for a name, title, office or division (try <em>Lisbon</em>, <em>Guide</em> or <em>Technology</em>) and press Enter: the matches stay, together with every manager above them, so the tree never loses its root. Vacant posts keep their place and their reports, finance, HR and marketing partners show their second, dotted-line manager under Also reports to, and the Name column stays put while you scroll sideways. The rating is a read-only <code>RatingControl</code> inside a column template.</p></Description>
            <Controls>
                <TextBoxControl Value="@_search" ValueChanged="Search" Placeholder="Name, title, office or division" Width="240px" />
            </Controls>
            <Demo>
                <TreeGridControl @key="_orgGeneration"
                                 TValue="StaffMember"
                                 DataSource="@_shown"
                                 IdMapping="Id"
                                 ParentIdMapping="ManagerId"
                                 TreeColumnIndex="0"
                                 EnableCollapseAll="true"
                                 InitialExpansionPredicate="@(p => !string.IsNullOrEmpty(_search) || p.Level < 1)"
                                 AllowSorting="true"
                                 AllowSelection="true"
                                 ToggleOnRowClick="false"
                                 Height="440px">
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="@nameof(StaffMember.Name)" HeaderText="Name" Width="290px" IsFrozen="true">
                        <Template>
                            @{ var p = (StaffMember)context; }
                            @if (p.Vacant) { <em class="vacant">Vacant</em> } else { <strong>@p.Name</strong> }
                            @if (p.OnLeave) { <span class="tag">on leave</span> }
                        </Template>
                    </TreeGridColumn>
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="@nameof(StaffMember.Title)" HeaderText="Title" Width="230px" />
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="@nameof(StaffMember.Office)" HeaderText="Office" Width="110px" />
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="@nameof(StaffMember.Headcount)" HeaderText="People below" Width="110px" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right">
                        <Template>@(((StaffMember)context).Headcount is > 0 and var n ? n.ToString("N0") : "")</Template>
                    </TreeGridColumn>
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="@nameof(StaffMember.Grade)" HeaderText="Grade" Width="70px" TextAlign="TextAlign.Center" />
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="@nameof(StaffMember.Contract)" HeaderText="Contract" Width="160px">
                        <Template>
                            @{ var p = (StaffMember)context; }
                            @p.Contract@(p.Fte < 1 ? $", {p.Fte:0.0} FTE" : "")
                        </Template>
                    </TreeGridColumn>
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="@nameof(StaffMember.Salary)" HeaderText="Salary" Width="100px" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Format="C0" />
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="@nameof(StaffMember.Rating)" HeaderText="Rating" Width="120px">
                        <Template>
                            @{ var p = (StaffMember)context; }
                            @if (p.Rating is { } stars) { <RatingControl Value="@stars" ReadOnly="true" /> }
                            else if (!p.Vacant) { <span class="muted">new starter</span> }
                        </Template>
                    </TreeGridColumn>
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="@nameof(StaffMember.Started)" HeaderText="Started" Width="100px" TextAlign="TextAlign.Center" Format="yyyy-MM-dd" />
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="@nameof(StaffMember.DottedLineId)" HeaderText="Also reports to" Width="190px">
                        <Template>@DottedLine((StaffMember)context)</Template>
                    </TreeGridColumn>
                </TreeGridControl>
                <p class="result">@OrgStatus</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
